WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.410
Three closed cans each hold three
hundred and thirty millilitres.

2
00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:09.090
Unroll each one into its net:
two circles and a rectangle.

3
00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:12.060
The tall can needs lots of curved side.

4
00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:15.080
The wide can needs two big ends.

5
00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:19.670
So of all the closed cans holding
three hundred and thirty millilitres,

6
00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:22.040
which uses the least metal?

7
00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:24.480
In this mission, you'll
find stationary points,

8
00:00:24.530 --> 00:00:29.390
where the tangent is horizontal, and
tell a local minimum from a maximum.

9
00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:33.810
Then you'll use the fixed volume to
write the metal in just one variable, and

10
00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:35.270
differentiate.

11
00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:39.960
Your mission: find the shape of can that
uses the least metal for three hundred

12
00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:41.400
and thirty millilitres.
